# `{ ...point, x }` allocates the new object with the layout of the literal, copies the slots and the order word of `point` inline where it has that layout, and then stores `x` into its slot.
# The store first asks whether the copy has filled that slot. Any other `point` is copied by one operation on the rare path.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="movedTo" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[copy]] = Patchpoint({{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK: Load({{*}}AOTObject_shapeWord{{*}}:TryCopyFields)
# CHECK: Store(b@{{*}}, b@[[copy]], offset = 8, ControlDependent|Writes:OrderWords{{*}}:TryCopyFields)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[old]] = Load(b@[[copy]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:PutSlotOrAdd)
# CHECK: Branch(b@{{*}}, Terminal, {{*}}:PutSlotOrAdd)
# CHECK: Store(b@{{*}}, b@[[copy]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:PutSlotOrAdd)
# CHECK-NEXT: Return(b@[[copy]], Terminal)
# CHECK: Patchpoint(b@[[copy]]:ColdAny, b@{{*}}:ColdAny, {{*}}:CopyDataProperties)
# CHECK-NOT: :CopyDataProperties)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
